{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/thm-buchberger","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:buchberger","kind":"theorem","title":"Buchberger's theorem over commutative rings","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-groebner-basis","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prop-s-polynomial-decomposition"],"proofs":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-buchberger"],"tags":["groebner-basis","buchberger","s-polynomial"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.buchberger","text":"buchberger.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/buchberger.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:buchberger\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative ring with unity, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra which\nis free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> an\n<a href=\"#def:admissible-system\">admissible system</a>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I \\leq A</code> be an\nideal generated by a unital set\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G := \\{g_\\gamma \\mid \\gamma \\in \\Gamma\\}</code>.</p>\n<p>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> is a <a href=\"#def:groebner-basis\">Gröbner--Shirshov basis</a> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> if and\nonly if all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code>-polynomials for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> have zero remainder under the\n<a href=\"#def:division-algorithm\">division algorithm</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/buchberger.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Theorem","number":"2.4.5"}
